ccalzone@general.math.uwaterloo.ca (Christopher Calzonetti) writes:
> I don't know if this is a bug or not, but I thought I'd see what others 
> think:
> 
> In a shop with a potion of oil in it, if I light the unpaid for potion, I 
> get charged a usage fee, plus the cost of the potion.
> 
> However, before I pay for the potion, it already loses its unpaid status.  
> If I immediately drop it again, I'm asked if I want to sell it back to the 
> store, even though I haven't paid for it yet.  (And according to the 
> shopkeeper, I still need to.)
> 
> Anyone else confirm this?  Is it a bug?

It looks reasonable to me. Ownership of the potion has transferred to
you, in exchange for its cost being placed on your bill. Since it's
now your potion, you can do what you like with it (including selling
it back); the bill remains to be settled, however. (Effectively, the
shopkeeper is treating the unlit and lit potions as two completely
different objects, as he's required to by the rules of the Yendorian
Fuel Tax.)

